# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Moved from an inline build.sh
# --check block by the .step series (batch 4: the next slowest blocks,
# measured one at a time on lenovinha). As a .step it is no build.sh edit, so it
# never makes intake HEAVY; it runs in the pool (it writes only its own scratch).
#
# ORDER 1916-tsel — `./build.sh --changed` selects by declared input. The
# fixture mutates a stub tree one path at a time: an input selects its
# fixture and not an unrelated one, a crate selects its reverse
# dependents, and a guard or an unmapped path selects everything.
STEP_DESC="Checking --changed selects checks by their inputs (1916-tsel)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-gate-changed-selects-by-input.sh"
STEP_ERROR="./build.sh --changed no longer scopes by input, or no longer fails safe to the full gate (1916-tsel)"
STEP_OK="--changed selects checks by their inputs passed"
